#!/usr/bin/env python3
# civ5-mod -- Civ V Mod Installer, Linux (Proton) edition of KekModInstaller.exe.
#
#   ./civ5-mod                         full-screen installer (same as `tui`)
#   ./civ5-mod status                  what's installed, updates, checks
#   ./civ5-mod install kekmod          latest release (also: tournament, lekmod)
#   ./civ5-mod install kekmod --version v2.0
#   ./civ5-mod uninstall kekmod
#   ./civ5-mod versions kekmod         list published releases
#   ./civ5-mod eui install [eui|xits]  / eui uninstall
#   ./civ5-mod lobby install | uninstall  civ5-lobby-patch (worldwide lobby list)
#   ./civ5-mod verify                  checks + unrecognized mod folders
#   ./civ5-mod clear-cache             shader caches + Civ V's cached DBs
#   ./civ5-mod redownload              delete the game, have Steam fetch it
#   ./civ5-mod kill | open             force close Civ V / open DLC folder
#   ./civ5-mod settings --beta on      persistent settings
#   ./civ5-mod self-update
#   ./civ5-mod install-self | uninstall-self
#   (see --help, or `<command> --help`)
#
# Players install it with one line; afterwards it's just `civ5-mod`:
#   curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/OBLASTWAR/kek-mod/main/installer/linux/civ5-mod | python3 - install-self
#
# Mirrors installer/*.cs feature for feature: three mutually exclusive mods,
# each with its bonus map (Fish Map Script / Better Pangaea / Lekmap), the two
# bundled EUI variants, the lobby patch, VERIFY MODS, CLEAR GFX CACHE, REDOWNLOAD CIV, the beta
# setting and self-update. Where Windows and Linux differ:
#
#   * The game is found through Steam's libraryfolders.vdf (native, ~/.steam,
#     Flatpak, Snap) instead of the registry, and must be the Windows build
#     running under Proton -- KEK Mod replaces a Windows DLL.
#   * Civ V's Documents folder lives inside the Proton prefix
#     (steamapps/compatdata/8930/pfx/...).
#   * EUI isn't fetchable from anywhere stable (see EuiExtra.cs), so it comes
#     from the same bundled zips the Windows build embeds: they're read straight
#     out of installer/KekModInstaller.exe (this checkout's copy, else the one
#     on main), so the exact-match check compares against identical bytes.
#   * Every mod ships a ui_check.bat. BatchScript below runs the small subset
#     of batch those scripts use (copy/xcopy, del, IF EXIST, FIND/FINDSTR, set,
#     one PowerShell string replace), sandboxed to Assets/DLC, with Windows'
#     case-insensitive path lookups.
#   * Shader caches are Linux/Proton ones (Steam's per-game cache, DXVK, Mesa,
#     NVIDIA) plus the Windows-side ones inside the prefix.
#
# Needs only python3 (3.8+, standard library). Settings live in
# ~/.config/civ5-mod, downloads are cached in ~/.cache/civ5-mod.
# Set GITHUB_TOKEN to lift GitHub's 60 requests/hour anonymous limit.

